  "question": {
    "text": "The vapour pressure of water at T (K) is 20 mm Hg. The following solutions are prepared at T (K)<br />\rI. 6 g of urea (molecular weight = 60) is dissolved in 178.2 g of water.<br />\rII. 0.01 mol of glucose is dissolved in 179.82 g of water.<br />\rIII. 5.3 g of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> (molecular weight = 106) is dissolved in 179.1 g of water.<br />\rIdentify the correct order in which the vapour pressure of solutions increases"
  },
  "options": [
